{
  "_comment": [
    "Localized command names, as a Spanish AutoCAD spells them -- checked on",
    "2026-09-27 against Autodesk's Spanish help (each command page is titled",
    "with its localized name, e.g. POL (comando)) and a stock Spanish acad.pgp.",
    "A command the Spanish AutoCAD keeps in English (RECTANG, DIST, LIST) has",
    "no entry here: its English name already works. Nor has PLINE: the",
    "Spanish name is POL, which the English acad.pgp already gives to POLYGON",
    "-- English wins; a Spanish user adds 'POL, *PLINE' to their acad.pgp",
    "(Tools > Customize > Edit Program Parameters). English never",
    "stops working: L, LINE and _LINE all draw a line with this file active.",
    "A name that shadows an English command or alias is refused by the loader",
    "(core/i18n/commands.py) and by tests/test_i18n_commands.py, so adding one",
    "cannot cost anybody a command. Corrections welcome -- if your AutoCAD",
    "spells one differently, change the name and nothing else."
  ],

